Sure! For this special dinner party, I would choose Leonardo da Vinci, Marie Curie, Albert Einstein, and Isaac Newton. It’s always fascinating to hear these individuals' thoughts and to learn about their perspectives on their scientific discoveries and achievements.

Leonardo Da Vinci would be the first historical figure I pick for such a hypothetical get together. This iconic artist, inventor, scientist, and polymath of the Renaissance era fascinates me endlessly with his boundless creativity and innovative spirit. His contributions range from painting masterpieces like 'The Last Supper' to groundbreaking work in science, including early insights into hydrodynamics.

Marie Curie, a monumental figure in not just her own time, but throughout the annals of modern history. She represents an epitome of dedication and passion for research and is celebrated for her pioneering contribution that established radiation as a tool for diagnosing and treating medical illnesses. Notably, she was the first woman to receive the Nobel Prize and has been awarded two;
